/// Synopsis: the documented limits of the animations, each next to its way out where it has one: a `#pause` between the lines of a `>` box shows the box whole on the first step (its bottom edge lightly veiled) and holds back only what follows it; quotations on consecutive lines show on the first step as plain text in quotation marks, while quotations separated by blank lines are revealed one per step; with this theme, Touying's `#item-by-item` shows every item on every step; a `#speaker-note` glued to the items shows the covered item, because Touying puts the note before the covered part and the veil of the theme gets no height there (the note after a blank line does not); a covered line glued to a visible one and followed by a shape, or by an image, shows on the first step (the `#pause` in a paragraph of its own veils it); a `#pause` in a column covers the next column badly: its callout is veiled in bands, its shape and its image not at all, and a list alone in it is veiled but written as plain text (`->`) or keeps its markers unveiled (`-`) (`#uncover("2-")` around the content of the next columns veils it whole, also on a third step); an `#uncover` around an item after another item of a list, glued to it or after a blank line, does not veil it (a `#pause` between the items does); in a list right inside an `#align(center)` or an `#align(right)` the marker of the covered item stands next to its text on the first step and goes to the left margin on the next, as in Touying's own themes (the list as a block, `#align(center, block(align(left)[..]))` or the same with `right`, keeps it in place); a `#pause` and an `#uncover` in one paragraph: Touying moves the covered part, and the first step reads "First. Third. Second. Fourth." (one paragraph each keeps the order); a list split by a `#pause` counts from 1 under a `#set enum(start: 3)` (the first number written keeps it). The other limits are tested elsewhere: "Unsupported mark" in `tests/errors/`, the covered content that runs on to the next page in `sections/pause-overflow`.
#import "../../common.typ": *
#show: setup
#include "body.typ"
